From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] module-x11-bell: make the X11 I/O error handler idempotent

libX11 can invoke the per-display I/O error exit handler more than once
for a single dead connection: _XEventsQueued() tests XlibDisplayIOError
only on entry, then _XSend() flushes buffered requests and calls
_XIOError() when the write fails; _XReadEvents() then fails as well and
_XIOError() is entered a second time. _XIOError() does not exit and does
not guard against re-entry.

The handler destroyed impl->source and cleared the pointer only
afterwards, so the second invocation passed NULL to
pw_loop_destroy_source(). loop_destroy_source() then evaluates
spa_assert(s->impl == object) on a NULL source and crashes, which happens
reliably when a session's Xwayland goes away, e.g. when the gdm greeter
is torn down at login.

Only destroy the source while it is still valid, matching
module_destroy().

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-19
---
 src/modules/module-x11-bell.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/module-x11-bell.c b/src/modules/module-x11-bell.c
index 3e36607..493e217 100644
--- a/src/modules/module-x11-bell.c
+++ b/src/modules/module-x11-bell.c
@@ -161,8 +161,12 @@ static void x11_io_error_exit_handler(Display *display, void *data)
 
 	pw_log_warn("X11 display (%s) has encountered a fatal I/O error", DisplayString(display));
 
-	pw_loop_destroy_source(impl->loop, impl->source);
-	impl->source = NULL;
+	/* _XIOError() can be entered more than once for the same dead
+	 * connection, so only destroy the source while it is still valid */
+	if (impl->source) {
+		pw_loop_destroy_source(impl->loop, impl->source);
+		impl->source = NULL;
+	}
 
 	pw_impl_module_schedule_destroy(impl->module);
 }
